ardiographic evaluation of systolic and diastolic function in rats</article-title><source>J Am Soc Echocardiogr</source><year>2006</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1520</fpage><lpage>1525</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17138038</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.echo.2006.06.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pagel</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmeling</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kampine</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Warltier</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alteration of canine left ventricular diastolic function by intravenous anesthetics in vivo: ketamine and propofol</article-title><source>Anesthesiology</source><year>1992</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>419</fpage><lpage>425</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1539854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokumai</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishikage</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Otani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lang</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Age-related changes in left ventricular twist assessed by two-dimensional speckle-tracking imaging</article-title><source>J Am Soc Echocardiogr</source><year>2006</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1077</fpage><lpage>1084</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16950461</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.echo.2006.04.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serri</surname><given-names>K<